Feature: The screen of the TX15
  The screen of the TX15 shows what ArduPilot reports, from the telemetry on the serial line. The
  lamps along the top show the flight mode and whether the plane is armed. Below them are the air
  data, the horizon and the data for navigation. Use the screen to check each action: when you
  press a button or a switch, you see the plane answer on the radio itself.

  Expectation: The screen shows that the plane is armed
    Given the arm switch is off
    And the vehicle is disarmed
    And the TX15 screen arming is disarmed
    When the arm switch is on
    Then the vehicle is armed
    And the TX15 screen arming is armed

  Expectation: The screen shows the flight mode
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the arm switch is on
    When the mode switch is QLOITER
    Then the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    And the TX15 screen mode is QLOITER

  Expectation: The throttle stick lifts the plane on the serial line
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    And the plane is on the ground
    When the throttle stick is high
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the plane is flying
    And the height above home is at least 15 m

  Expectation: The screen shows forward flight
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the flight is hovering
    And the plane is flying
    And the height above home is at least 15 m
    And the throttle stick is high
    When the pilot switches to forward flight
    Then the flight is cruising
    And the autopilot mode is FBWA
    And the TX15 screen mode is FBWA

  Expectation: The aileron stick banks the plane on the serial line
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the autopilot mode is FBWA
    And the flight is cruising
    When the aileron stick is right
    Then the VTOL's wings are banked

  Expectation: The wings become level again on the serial line
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the autopilot mode is FBWA
    And the aileron stick is right
    And the VTOL's wings are banked
    When the aileron stick is centred
    Then the VTOL's wings are level

  Expectation: The screen shows the plane back in a hover
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the autopilot mode is FBWA
    And the flight is cruising
    When the pilot switches back to a hover
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    And the TX15 screen mode is QLOITER

  Expectation: The screen shows the plane landed and disarmed
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the plane is flying
    When the pilot sends the plane home
    Then the autopilot mode is QRTL
    And the plane is on the ground
    And the last landing is soft
    And the TX15 screen arming is disarmed
